# Always deploy to VPS

When finishing a change that affects the live game (client `public/game.js` / `public/index.html`, `server.js`, assets, SW/manifest, etc.):

1. Commit only the relevant files (never `accounts.json`).
2. Push to `origin/main`.
3. Deploy via plink: host `45.155.102.148`, key `C:\Users\tengo\Desktop\sksks.ppk`, path `/root/asteroids`.
4. On VPS: `git checkout -- public/asset-manifest.json` if dirty, `git pull --ff-only`, `npm run manifest`, `pm2 restart asteroids`.
5. Bump `game.js?v=` in `public/index.html` when shipping client JS.
   Client static files live under `public/` (server serves that as the web root).

Do this by default — do not wait for the user to say “push to vps”.
